{"id":"NAM","name":"Nahum","chapters":[{"number":1,"verses":[{"number":1,"text":"This is the burden against Nineveh, the book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite:","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":2,"text":"The LORD is a jealous and avenging God; the LORD is avenging and full of wrath. The LORD takes vengeance on His foes and reserves wrath for His enemies.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":130,"end":135,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":3,"text":"The LORD is slow to anger and great in power; the LORD will by no means leave the guilty unpunished. His path is in the whirlwind and storm, and clouds are the dust beneath His feet.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":4,"text":"He rebukes the sea and dries it up; He makes all the rivers run dry. Bashan and Carmel wither, and the flower of Lebanon wilts.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":5,"text":"The mountains quake before Him, and the hills melt away; the earth trembles at His presence— the world and all its dwellers.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":6,"text":"Who can withstand His indignation? Who can endure His burning anger? His wrath is poured out like fire; even rocks are shattered before Him.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":7,"text":"The LORD is good, a stronghold in the day of distress; He cares for those who trust in Him.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":8,"text":"But with an overwhelming flood He will make an end of Nineveh and pursue His enemies into darkness.","notes":[{"at":61,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"1:8 Literally of her place","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["1:8 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Literally "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["of her place"]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":51,"end":61,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":9,"text":"Whatever you plot against the LORD, He will bring to an end. Affliction will not rise up a second time.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":10,"text":"For they will be entangled as with thorns and consumed like the drink of a drunkard — like stubble that is fully dry.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":11,"text":"From you, O Nineveh, comes forth a plotter of evil against the LORD, a counselor of wickedness.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":10,"end":19,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":12,"text":"This is what the LORD says: “Though they are allied and numerous, yet they will be cut down and pass away. Though I have afflicted you, O Judah, I will afflict you no longer.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":136,"end":143,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":13,"text":"For I will now break their yoke from your neck and tear away your shackles.”","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":14,"text":"The LORD has issued a command concerning you, O Nineveh: “There will be no descendants to carry on your name. I will cut off the carved image and cast idol from the house of your gods; I will prepare your grave, for you are contemptible.”","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":46,"end":55,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":15,"text":"Look to the mountains— the feet of one who brings good news, who proclaims peace! Celebrate your feasts, O Judah; fulfill your vows. For the wicked will never again march through you; they will be utterly cut off.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]}],"headings":[{"afterVerse":null,"style":"s1","text":"The Burden against Nineveh","content":["The Burden against Nineveh"]},{"afterVerse":null,"style":"r","text":"(Jonah 1:1–3)","content":["(",{"type":"ref","loc":"JON 1:1-3","content":["Jonah 1:1–3"]},")"]}],"paragraphs":[{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":0,"end":82}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":82,"end":82},{"verse":2,"start":0,"end":39}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":40,"end":79}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":80,"end":116}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":117,"end":152}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":152,"end":152},{"verse":3,"start":0,"end":25}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":26,"end":45}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":46,"end":71}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":72,"end":100}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":101,"end":140}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":141,"end":182}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":182,"end":182},{"verse":4,"start":0,"end":35}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":36,"end":68}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":69,"end":94}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":95,"end":127}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":127,"end":127},{"verse":5,"start":0,"end":31}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":32,"end":56}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":57,"end":92}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":93,"end":124}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":124,"end":124},{"verse":6,"start":0,"end":34}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":6,"start":35,"end":68}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":6,"start":69,"end":103}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":6,"start":104,"end":140}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":6,"start":140,"end":140},{"verse":7,"start":0,"end":17}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":18,"end":54}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":55,"end":91}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":91,"end":91},{"verse":8,"start":0,"end":30}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":31,"end":61}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":62,"end":99}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":99,"end":99},{"verse":9,"start":0,"end":35}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":36,"end":60}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":61,"end":88}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":89,"end":103}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":103,"end":103},{"verse":10,"start":0,"end":41}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":42,"end":85}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":86,"end":117}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":117,"end":117},{"verse":11,"start":0,"end":32}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":33,"end":68}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":69,"end":95}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":95,"end":95},{"verse":12,"start":0,"end":27}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":28,"end":65}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":66,"end":106}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":107,"end":144}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":145,"end":174}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":174,"end":174},{"verse":13,"start":0,"end":46}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":47,"end":76}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":76,"end":76},{"verse":14,"start":0,"end":56}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":57,"end":86}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":87,"end":109}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":110,"end":155}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":156,"end":184}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":185,"end":211}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":212,"end":238}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":14,"start":238,"end":238},{"verse":15,"start":0,"end":22}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":15,"start":23,"end":60}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":15,"start":61,"end":81}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":15,"start":82,"end":113}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":15,"start":114,"end":132}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":15,"start":133,"end":183}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":15,"start":184,"end":213}]}],"offsetUnit":"unicode-codepoint"},{"number":2,"verses":[{"number":1,"text":"One who scatters advances against you, O Nineveh. Guard the fortress! Watch the road! Brace yourselves! Summon all your strength!","notes":[{"at":103,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"2:1 Hebrew Strengthen your loins!","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["2:1 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Hebrew "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["Strengthen your loins!"]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":39,"end":48,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":2,"text":"For the LORD will restore the splendor of Jacob like the splendor of Israel, though destroyers have laid them waste and ruined the branches of their vine.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":3,"text":"The shields of his mighty men are red; the valiant warriors are dressed in scarlet. The fittings of the chariots flash like fire on the day they are prepared, and the spears of cypress have been brandished.","notes":[{"at":206,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"2:3 Hebrew; alternately, the spears may be of pine or juniper or fir; LXX and Syriac they are prepared, and the horsemen rush to and fro.","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["2:3 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Hebrew; alternately, the spears may be of "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["pine "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["juniper "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["fir"]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["; LXX and Syriac "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["they are prepared, and the horsemen rush to and fro."]}]}],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":4,"text":"The chariots dash through the streets; they rush around the plazas, appearing like torches, darting about like lightning.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":5,"text":"He summons his nobles; they stumble as they advance. They race to its wall; the protective shield is set in place.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":6,"text":"The river gates are thrown open and the palace collapses.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":7,"text":"It is decreed that the city be exiled and carried away; her maidservants moan like doves, and beat upon their breasts.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":19,"end":27,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":8,"text":"Nineveh has been like a pool of water throughout her days, but now it is draining away. “Stop! Stop!” they cry, but no one turns back.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":9,"text":"“Plunder the silver! Plunder the gold!” There is no end to the treasure, an abundance of every precious thing.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":10,"text":"She is emptied! Yes, she is desolate and laid waste! Hearts melt, knees knock, bodies tremble, and every face grows pale!","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":11,"text":"Where is the lions’ lair or the feeding ground of the young lions, where the lion and lioness prowled with their cubs, with nothing to frighten them away?","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":107,"end":112,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":12,"text":"The lion mauled enough for its cubs and strangled prey for the lioness. It filled its dens with the kill, and its lairs with mauled prey.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":13,"text":"“Behold, I am against you,” declares the LORD of Hosts. “I will reduce your chariots to cinders, and the sword will devour your young lions. I will cut off your prey from the earth, and the voices of your messengers will no longer be heard.”","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]}],"headings":[{"afterVerse":null,"style":"s1","text":"The Overthrow of Nineveh","content":["The Overthrow of Nineveh"]}],"paragraphs":[{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":0,"end":25}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":26,"end":49}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":50,"end":69}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":70,"end":85}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":86,"end":103}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":104,"end":129}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":129,"end":129},{"verse":2,"start":0,"end":47}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":48,"end":76}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":77,"end":115}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":116,"end":154}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":154,"end":154},{"verse":3,"start":0,"end":38}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":39,"end":83}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":84,"end":128}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":129,"end":158}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":159,"end":184}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":185,"end":206}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":206,"end":206},{"verse":4,"start":0,"end":38}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":39,"end":67}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":68,"end":91}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":92,"end":121}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":4,"start":121,"end":121},{"verse":5,"start":0,"end":22}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":23,"end":52}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":53,"end":75}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":76,"end":114}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":5,"start":114,"end":114},{"verse":6,"start":0,"end":31}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":6,"start":32,"end":57}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":6,"start":57,"end":57},{"verse":7,"start":0,"end":37}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":38,"end":55}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":56,"end":89}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":90,"end":118}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":118,"end":118},{"verse":8,"start":0,"end":37}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":38,"end":58}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":59,"end":87}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":88,"end":111}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":112,"end":134}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":8,"start":134,"end":134},{"verse":9,"start":0,"end":20}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":21,"end":39}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":40,"end":72}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":73,"end":110}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":110,"end":110},{"verse":10,"start":0,"end":15}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":16,"end":52}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":53,"end":78}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":79,"end":121}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":10,"start":121,"end":121},{"verse":11,"start":0,"end":24}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":25,"end":66}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":67,"end":118}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":119,"end":154}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":11,"start":154,"end":154},{"verse":12,"start":0,"end":35}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":36,"end":71}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":72,"end":105}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":106,"end":137}]},{"style":"b","spans":[]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":137,"end":137},{"verse":13,"start":0,"end":27}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":28,"end":55}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":56,"end":96}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":97,"end":140}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":141,"end":181}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":182,"end":215}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":13,"start":216,"end":241}]}],"offsetUnit":"unicode-codepoint"},{"number":3,"verses":[{"number":1,"text":"Woe to the city of blood, full of lies, full of plunder, never without prey.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":2,"text":"The crack of the whip, the rumble of the wheel, galloping horse and bounding chariot!","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":3,"text":"Charging horseman, flashing sword, shining spear; heaps of slain, mounds of corpses, dead bodies without end— they stumble over their dead—","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":4,"text":"because of the many harlotries of the harlot, the seductive mistress of sorcery, who betrays nations by her prostitution and clans by her witchcraft.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":5,"text":"“Behold, I am against you,” declares the LORD of Hosts. “I will lift your skirts over your face. I will show your nakedness to the nations and your shame to the kingdoms.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":11,"end":13,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":6,"text":"I will pelt you with filth and treat you with contempt; I will make a spectacle of you.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":7,"text":"Then all who see you will recoil from you and say, ‘Nineveh is devastated; who will grieve for her?’ Where can I find comforters for you?”","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":8,"text":"Are you better than Thebes, stationed by the Nile with water around her, whose rampart was the sea, whose wall was the water?","notes":[{"at":27,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:8 Hebrew No-amon","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:8 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Hebrew "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["No-amon"]}]}],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":9,"text":"Cush and Egypt were her boundless strength; Put and Libya were her allies.","notes":[{"at":4,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:9 That is, the upper Nile region","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:9 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["That is, the upper Nile region"]}]}],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":10,"text":"Yet she became an exile; she went into captivity. Her infants were dashed to pieces at the head of every street. They cast lots for her dignitaries, and all her nobles were bound in chains.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":11,"text":"You too will become drunk; you will go into hiding and seek refuge from the enemy.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":12,"text":"All your fortresses are fig trees with the first ripe figs; when shaken, they fall into the mouth of the eater!","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":13,"text":"Look at your troops — they are like your women! The gates of your land are wide open to your enemies; fire consumes their bars.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":14,"text":"Draw your water for the siege; strengthen your fortresses. Work the clay and tread the mortar; repair the brick kiln!","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":112,"end":116,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":15,"text":"There the fire will devour you; the sword will cut you down and consume you like a young locust. Make yourself many like the young locust; make yourself many like the swarming locust!","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":16,"text":"You have multiplied your merchants more than the stars of the sky. The young locust strips the land and flies away.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":17,"text":"Your guards are like the swarming locust, and your scribes like clouds of locusts that settle on the walls on a cold day. When the sun rises, they fly away, and no one knows where.","notes":[{"at":11,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:17 Or princes","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:17 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["princes"]}]},{"at":58,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:17 Or marshals","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:17 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["marshals"]}]}],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":18,"text":"O king of Assyria, your shepherds slumber; your officers sleep. Your people are scattered on the mountains with no one to gather them.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":19,"text":"There is no healing for your injury; your wound is severe. All who hear the news of you applaud your downfall, for who has not experienced your constant cruelty?","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":101,"end":109,"marker":"add"}]}],"headings":[{"afterVerse":null,"style":"s1","text":"Judgment on Nineveh","content":["Judgment on Ni